WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.107 --> 00:00:04.100
- Unholiest of spirits, we offer thee

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.033
a life for a life.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.490
Oh, mighty dark Lord,

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:12.900
by whom all is set to fire,
(chanting in foreign language)

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.290
thy power be thy path,

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.463
thy will my desire.

00:00:20.538 --> 00:00:23.538
(suspenseful music)

00:00:26.967 --> 00:00:27.800
- Sabrina,

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.570
are you sure about this?

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:33.903
- I have to be.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.030
(whimpers)

00:00:41.155 --> 00:00:43.072
(thud)

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.150
- The hounds invoked.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:50.930
- [All] The door opened.

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:54.012
The price paid in blood.

00:00:54.012 --> 00:00:55.083
Thomas Kinkle,

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.100
we entreat thee.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.530
Rise!

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:00.363
Rise!

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.657
Rise!

00:01:02.657 --> 00:01:05.657
(suspenseful music)

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:14.225
- [Sabrina] Tommy?

00:01:14.225 --> 00:01:17.230
(door bangs shut)

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:18.620
- He won't answer you.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.337
- How's he doing?

00:01:20.337 --> 00:01:21.650
(sighs)

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:22.483
- I'll show you.

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:26.443
Watch.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:28.653
- Oh my god!

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.620
- At first,

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.380
I thought he was getting better,

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:36.580
that he was remembering.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:39.760
That's all he'll do.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.233
React.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:43.953
Like a robot.

00:01:46.838 --> 00:01:48.921
(puking)

00:01:55.331 --> 00:01:57.581
(coughing)

00:01:59.496 --> 00:02:01.663
(gasping)

00:02:02.656 --> 00:02:05.196
- Welcome back, sister.

00:02:05.196 --> 00:02:07.196
(gasps)

00:02:09.396 --> 00:02:10.479
- Where am I?

00:02:11.726 --> 00:02:13.410
Where was I?

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:15.430
- So you didn't kill her?

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:16.830
- We did.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.824
But only because Sabrina had
a plan to bring Agatha back.

00:02:19.824 --> 00:02:21.510
- [All] Thy power be the path,

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:23.440
thy will be my desire,

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.810
in hell as it is on earth.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:26.798
Praise Satan.

00:02:26.798 --> 00:02:27.713
Amen.

00:02:30.071 --> 00:02:31.490
(Agatha gagging)

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:32.980
- Agatha?

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.431
Agatha, what's the matter?

00:02:34.431 --> 00:02:36.514
(coughs)

00:02:37.431 --> 00:02:39.970
(vomits)

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:41.763
- See this thing ain't Tommy.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.808
I don't know what the hell
it is, but it ain't my son.

00:02:45.808 --> 00:02:47.388
(suspenseful music)

00:02:47.388 --> 00:02:48.638
And if you are,

00:02:50.048 --> 00:02:52.068
you might as well have
stayed in the mines.

00:02:52.068 --> 00:02:52.901
- Help me.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.497
(thud)

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.350
- [Man] How did Agatha
end up a living cadaver?

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:06.513
Tell me everything.

00:03:06.513 --> 00:03:09.569
- The witch they killed

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:10.803
and brought back to life

00:03:10.803 --> 00:03:13.700
is getting sicker, and sicker.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:15.520
That's the Grim Reaper doing it to her.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:16.560
He's expecting her body.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.320
Her suffering won't end until
there's one in the ground.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.400
Until balance is restored.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.210
There's so fixing it, Sabrina.

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:24.801
You've opened Pandora's Box.

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:27.801
(suspenseful music)

00:03:28.888 --> 00:03:31.638
(knobs clicking)

00:03:36.628 --> 00:03:38.400
(whirring)

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.733
(trickling)

00:03:46.253 --> 00:03:49.420
(electricity buzzing)

00:03:54.104 --> 00:03:56.354
(stomping)

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:00.053
(roaring)

00:04:00.053 --> 00:04:02.303
(rattling)

00:04:05.586 --> 00:04:07.655
(suspenseful music)

00:04:07.655 --> 00:04:09.515
(groaning)

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.895
(screams)

00:04:11.895 --> 00:04:12.728
- Sabrina?

00:04:13.995 --> 00:04:16.195
What's the matter?

00:04:16.195 --> 00:04:19.120
- When I solved the puzzle,
the Acheron configuration,

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:22.640
it set a demon free and now it's loose!

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.410
- Edward Spellman imprisoned me

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.654
in the Acheron puzzle for 70 years.

00:04:27.654 --> 00:04:30.170
I'll not be caged again!

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:31.810
- What do you want, Hellspawn?

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:32.913
- First,

00:04:33.908 --> 00:04:36.670
revenge on the family of Edward Spellman.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.130
- Did you have to ask, love?

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:39.900
- And then freedom!

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.030
So I may fill the world

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.905
with my sublime nightmares.

00:04:44.905 --> 00:04:47.488
(creepy music)

00:04:50.944 --> 00:04:53.111
(snoring)

00:04:57.491 --> 00:04:58.533
- Ambrose.

00:04:58.533 --> 00:04:59.677
Ambrose!

00:04:59.677 --> 00:05:01.260
- I'm awake, sorry!

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.080
- Nothing happened.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.630
The mandrake spell didn't work.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.850
So what do we do now?

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:08.683
- Sabrina.

00:05:10.737 --> 00:05:12.944
(gasps)

00:05:12.944 --> 00:05:15.944
(suspenseful music)

00:05:28.804 --> 00:05:30.143
You're not Sabrina.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:36.113
- What an awful thing to say.

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:39.435
(crackling)

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:44.030
(high pitched wail)

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:45.570
I know how to make you love me

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:48.993
and only me.

00:05:53.254 --> 00:05:55.671
(squelching)

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:01.134
(high pitched wail)

00:06:01.134 --> 00:06:02.900
Why won't you let me fix you?

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.810
- 'Cause I'm not broken!

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:05.643
- Theo.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.603
You're being awfully mean.

00:06:09.713 --> 00:06:12.130
(squelching)

00:06:13.512 --> 00:06:16.159
(high pitched wail)

00:06:16.159 --> 00:06:17.760
- It's not Sabrina, it's something else!

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.182
I saw it in one of my visions.

00:06:19.182 --> 00:06:21.180
Like a twin!

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.083
- Guys.

00:06:22.083 --> 00:06:25.083
(high pitched wail)

00:06:26.884 --> 00:06:28.863
- You murdered my friends?

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:30.713
- [Rosalind] Run!

00:06:30.713 --> 00:06:31.683
Run! Go!

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:37.830
- Remember, the Yule
Log is not a decoration.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.363
It is a protection.

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:43.850
It must burn continuously from now,

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:45.080
through the shortest day,

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:48.720
through the longest night, until dawn.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:51.720
Otherwise, Satan knows
what malevolent forces

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:53.570
might come down our chimney.

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:55.300
Creatures with, perhaps,

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:56.683
deadly intentions.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.573
So let's keep the log lit, shall we?

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:06.813
- Warden of the longest night,

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:10.813
Fae things fear the yule fire's light.

00:07:14.127 --> 00:07:15.893
But you'll find dead,

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.283
when portals laid bare.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.870
The darkness comes to trick

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.263
and to tear.

00:07:26.961 --> 00:07:29.128
(sizzles)

00:07:31.453 --> 00:07:33.326
(tense music)

00:07:33.326 --> 00:07:35.515
(chants in foreign language)

00:07:35.515 --> 00:07:37.143
(thud)

00:07:37.143 --> 00:07:40.143
(children laughing)

00:07:41.367 --> 00:07:42.534
- Who's there?

00:07:45.115 --> 00:07:48.756
(children laughing)

00:07:48.756 --> 00:07:50.404
♪ Have a holly jolly Christmas ♪

00:07:50.404 --> 00:07:53.154
(metal clinking)

00:07:55.515 --> 00:07:57.133
- Oh, that can't be good.

00:07:57.133 --> 00:07:57.966
(children laughing)

00:07:57.966 --> 00:08:01.049
(footsteps thudding)

00:08:04.851 --> 00:08:06.740
(gasps)

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:10.323
(sewing machine puttering)

00:08:19.951 --> 00:08:20.784
- Leticia.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:24.496
Leticia!

00:08:24.496 --> 00:08:25.430
(child laughing)

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:27.440
- So, it's not poltergeists.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.520
It's the Yule Lads.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:31.670
- Impish spirits of
children that come down

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:34.820
from the mountains every
midwinter to cause mischief

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:37.670
in the unguarded homes of witches.

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:40.720
They must have gotten in
when the yule fire went out.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:41.593
- Right, so we banish the buggers?

00:08:41.593 --> 00:08:43.860
- Well, that's not so easy, love.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:46.280
The Yule Lads are like bed bugs.

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:47.220
Once they get into your house,

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:49.158
they're very difficult to get rid of.

00:08:49.158 --> 00:08:50.654
- 'Brina,

00:08:50.654 --> 00:08:52.090
isn't there some

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:55.133
witchy way we could take care of Billy?

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:03.840
- The next time you guys are practicing,

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:05.980
tie a new knot on this cord.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:08.760
Billy will keep tripping over his feet.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:09.620
That'll bruise his ego.
(chuckles)

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:11.320
- Thanks, 'Brina, you're the best.

00:09:14.313 --> 00:09:16.800
(laughing)

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:18.460
Where is he?

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:19.477
Where's Billy?!

00:09:27.079 --> 00:09:27.912
- Billy!

00:09:27.912 --> 00:09:28.958
- Whoa!

00:09:28.958 --> 00:09:30.413
(thudding)

00:09:30.413 --> 00:09:32.712
(crack)

00:09:32.712 --> 00:09:35.545
(Billy screaming)

00:09:38.214 --> 00:09:41.214
(suspenseful music)

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.853
- Billy, you okay, man?

00:09:49.853 --> 00:09:51.679
Just stay cool.

00:09:51.679 --> 00:09:53.747
Give him some room.

00:09:53.747 --> 00:09:54.847
Breath.

00:09:54.847 --> 00:09:56.677
Someone go get the nurse or something.

00:09:56.677 --> 00:09:57.930
(shouting)

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:00.930
(suspenseful music)

00:10:03.587 --> 00:10:06.123
- Gendered spells of metamorphosis!

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:15.130
Okay, I mixed all the ingredients together

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:16.130
like the spell said.

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:19.550
Now what?

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.570
- Now it's time, Theo.

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:24.177
Are you ready to become?

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:28.663
- How will I know if the spell worked?

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:30.970
What if the Spellmans find out that I...

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:33.789
- Sleep, Theo.

00:10:33.789 --> 00:10:37.400
And dream of the boy you'll become.

00:10:40.566 --> 00:10:41.886
- Ow.

00:10:41.886 --> 00:10:44.636
(dramatic music)

00:10:57.474 --> 00:10:59.001
(knocking)

00:10:59.001 --> 00:11:00.790
- Ms. Spellman, are you home?

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:02.820
I might've done something really dumb.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:04.553
- Oh, sweet Satan!

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:08.290
- I broke in and then I
stole one of your spells

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:09.715
and I tried to make a
potion to help me transition

00:11:09.715 --> 00:11:12.270
and now I'm, uh-

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.420
- Petrifying into wood.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:17.323
Oh, my poor little Pinocchio in reverse.

00:11:18.273 --> 00:11:19.193
- Ow, ow!

00:11:19.193 --> 00:11:21.250
- I mean, that can happen
with plant-based spells.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:23.130
Botanicals are tricky.
- Is there any way to stop it?

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:24.230
- Oh yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:26.090
Well, yes and no.

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:26.963
It's mostly no.

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:31.730
- You sure about this?

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:35.630
- Okay, all right.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.509
So, have a nice little bite

00:11:37.509 --> 00:11:39.228
down on that.

00:11:39.228 --> 00:11:40.370
Good boy.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:42.127
And I'm gonna hold your hand, there we go.

00:11:42.127 --> 00:11:44.100
And we will have that arm off in no time.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.531
Chop, chop, as they say!

00:11:45.531 --> 00:11:48.180
(laughs nervously)

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:49.430
- Hold still for me, boy.

00:11:50.878 --> 00:11:53.230
(tense music)

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:54.063
Hold it.

00:11:57.347 --> 00:11:58.997
Nice and still for me now.

00:11:58.997 --> 00:12:03.997
(thudding)
(breathing heavily)

